  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Third COVID-19 Recovery and Resilience Development Policy Financing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Third COVID-19 Recovery and Resilience Development Policy Financing for S&#xe3;o TomE and Principe (STP) is to support the government&apos;s response to the human and economic impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and economy-wide and sectoral reforms for a stronger recovery. The programmatic series is organized around two pillars. Pillar 1 has the objective of mitigating the impacts of the COVID-19 crisis on lives and livelihoods and strengthening investment in human capital. Pillar 2 has the objective of mitigating the impact of the COVID-19 crisis on businesses and jobs and laying the foundations for sustainable economic growth. Furthermore, this operation is aligned with Government of STP (GoSTP&apos;s) climate change mitigation and adaptation objectives and will directly support STP&apos;s resilience to climate change related disasters and other shocks, including future pandemics.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this operation is to support the government&apos;s response to the human and economic impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and economy-wide and sectoral reforms for a stronger recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
