  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Domestic tax revenue as percentage of GDP</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-12-15" value="12.6" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-12-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-15"></period-end>
     <target value="&amp;gt;13">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Not met. Despite the successful implementation of the VAT in 2023, the difficult macroeconomic situation resulted in a weak tax-to-GDP ratio in 2023. However, the tax-to-GDP ratio is estimated to reach 12.9 percent in 2024, closer to the target.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="11.4"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coverage of the credit registry (percent of the adult population)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-12-15" value="14" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-12-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-15"></period-end>
     <target value="17">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Not met but continued progress achieved. However, due to revisions in population estimates, the baseline was revised downward, at 11.9 percent, instead of 14 percent at the time of the DPO. Hence the coverage did increase, though by a lesser extent than envisaged at the time (+1.1 percentage points (pp) versus a target of +3 pp compared to the baseline). Despite continuous increase, the RI still underperformed by October 2024, reaching 14.1 percent (and representing an increase by 2.2 pp compared to the baseline). The slower increase in the coverage is explained by technical issues at a large bank in terms of aligning IT systems with the Central Bank as well as delays integrating microfinance institutions associated with these institutions having to install new IT systems.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="13"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
